WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.696
Oxford Bookworms. Starters.
 
00:00:04.756 --> 00:00:11.292
The Fifteenth Character by Rosemary Border. Read by Nick Mercer.
 
00:00:11.352 --> 00:00:17.000
Published and Copyright Oxford University Press 2000.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:28.700
Chapter One. Jobs for Today.
 
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.500
Every day lots of different people come to Happy Hills 

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.114
because there are lots of exciting things to do.

00:00:39.174 --> 00:00:44.795
Sally Brown works at Happy Hills in her holiday.

00:00:44.855 --> 00:00:50.506
She is a student, and she wants to be a teacher.

00:00:50.566 --> 00:00:55.546
I need the money, she tells her family,

00:00:55.606 --> 00:00:58.888
and it’s an interesting job.

00:00:58.948 --> 00:01:05.141
But she is always very tired in the evening.

00:01:05.201 --> 00:01:11.802
The workers at Happy Hills arrive early in the morning.

00:01:11.862 --> 00:01:18.214
They all wear clean green trousers and yellow shirts.

00:01:18.274 --> 00:01:24.458
They must smile a lot and be nice to all the visitors.

00:01:24.518 --> 00:01:34.592
Every morning Mr Parry puts a list of Jobs for Today in the workers’ canteen.

00:01:34.652 --> 00:01:39.404
Mr Parry wears different clothes.

00:01:39.464 --> 00:01:45.800
His shirt is green and his trousers are white, 

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:52.307
and he wears a red coat with I’m Ken Parry.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.273
Can I help you?

00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:56.728
on his pocket.

00:01:56.788 --> 00:02:00.600
The visitors call him Ken, 

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:06.672
but all the workers call him Mr Parry.

00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:13.784
Today Sally arrives at Happy Hills at eight o'clock.

00:02:13.844 --> 00:02:19.100
On her shirt there is a picture of a smiling face 

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:25.621
and Have a Happy Day in black and red writing.

00:02:25.681 --> 00:02:33.280
She goes to the canteen and looks for Mr Parry's list.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:39.547
What job am I doing today? Sally thinks.
 
00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:46.368
Am I making tea, or helping in the children’s play house?

00:02:46.428 --> 00:02:49.971
But Sally is wrong.

00:02:50.030 --> 00:02:56.690
The list says, Sally Brown — Connie Cat.

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:02.038
Break: eleven o’clock.

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:08.622
Oh no! thinks Sally.
 
00:03:08.682 --> 00:03:18.845
Nobody likes wearing the costumes, but at Happy Hills the characters are very important.

00:03:18.905 --> 00:03:23.700
The visitors like to take photos of their children 

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:44.860
with Cowboy Joe, Charlie Clown, Baby Blue Eyes, Photo Phil, Big John, Connie Cat, Big Apple, Miss Flower, Edward Elephant and all their friends.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:50.859
Everybody always asks the same questions:

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:55.190
Are you very hot in your costume?

00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:00.251
and How do you eat and drink?

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:04.692
Edward Elephant has the best job.

00:04:04.752 --> 00:04:09.142
He has a bag of water under his costume.

00:04:09.202 --> 00:04:13.178
He can spray the visitors with water.

00:04:13.238 --> 00:04:20.579
And Photo Phil and Charlie Clown make everybody laugh.

00:04:20.639 --> 00:04:25.122
But Connie Cat cannot do that.

00:04:25.182 --> 00:04:33.428
She can only say "miaow" to the children all day.

00:04:33.488 --> 00:04:37.441
Sally looks for her costume.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:44.344
A tall man in a cowboy costume is standing beside her.

00:04:44.404 --> 00:04:49.185
Hullo, Sally, says the cowboy.
 
00:04:49.245 --> 00:04:52.427
It’s me — William.

00:04:52.486 --> 00:04:55.929
William is a student too.

00:04:55.988 --> 00:04:58.800
He is Sally's friend.

00:04:58.859 --> 00:05:03.093
Which costume are you looking for?

00:05:03.152 --> 00:05:05.794
Connie Cat.

00:05:05.854 --> 00:05:08.665
When’s your break?

00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:11.056
Eleven o’clock.

00:05:11.116 --> 00:05:15.031
Me too.

00:05:15.091 --> 00:05:27.600
Chapter Two. Here Comes Zapp!

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.611
It is nine o’clock.

00:05:29.671 --> 00:05:35.344
The doors open, but there are not many visitors today.

00:05:35.404 --> 00:05:41.968
They all have invitations, and they show them to Mr Parry.

00:05:42.028 --> 00:05:46.638
A very famous man is coming to Happy Hills.

00:05:46.698 --> 00:05:51.040
So Mr Parry is very excited.

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.642
Zapp’s coming today.

00:05:53.702 --> 00:05:57.054
He’s opening the new Zapp-o-copter,

00:05:57.114 --> 00:06:00.027
says William to Sally.

00:06:00.087 --> 00:06:04.631
Stop talking and do some work!

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:07.423
says Mr Parry.

00:06:07.483 --> 00:06:10.668
Zapp is a singer.

00:06:10.728 --> 00:06:17.824
Sally loves listening to his songs and she has all his CDs.

00:06:17.884 --> 00:06:22.768
There is a picture of him in her room too.

00:06:22.828 --> 00:06:27.800
The Zapp-o-copter is very exciting.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:35.427
People can sit in little helicopters and go up and down very fast.

00:06:35.487 --> 00:06:42.431
The visitors stand behind a blue rope and wait for Zapp.

00:06:42.491 --> 00:06:49.143
Please stay behind the rope, says Mr Parry.

00:06:49.203 --> 00:06:53.884
Suddenly there is a noise in the sky.

00:06:53.944 --> 00:06:56.465
Everybody looks up.

00:06:56.525 --> 00:07:02.337
It’s Zapp’s helicopter! says William.

00:07:02.397 --> 00:07:05.706
The helicopter comes down.

00:07:05.766 --> 00:07:08.405
And Zapp gets out.

00:07:08.464 --> 00:07:12.406
He smiles at the visitors.

00:07:12.466 --> 00:07:18.790
Oh — he’s wonderful! says a young girl.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:22.231
She gives Zapp a flower.

00:07:22.291 --> 00:07:29.124
He gives her a big smile and says, Thank you.

00:07:29.184 --> 00:07:34.333
Sally is hot and thirsty in her costume.

00:07:34.393 --> 00:07:42.055
She wants to talk too, but Mr Parry is watching.

00:07:42.115 --> 00:07:53.700
Chapter Three. Zapp’s New Song. 

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:59.340
Mr Parry takes the singer to the Zapp-o-copter.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.634
Zapp cuts the rope.

00:08:02.694 --> 00:08:05.139
Thank you, Zapp.

00:08:05.199 --> 00:08:09.262
Now please can you sing for us?

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:11.654
says Mr Parry.

00:08:11.714 --> 00:08:17.818
OK! But the people must help me! he says.

00:08:17.878 --> 00:08:20.610
He begins to sing.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:25.874
Everybody knows the song and sings it with him.

00:08:25.934 --> 00:08:29.867
Thank you, says Zapp.

00:08:29.926 --> 00:08:33.220
You’re all wonderful singers.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.492
Now look at this.

00:08:36.552 --> 00:08:40.233
He takes a CD out of his pocket.

00:08:40.293 --> 00:08:46.046
This is my new song, he says.

00:08:46.106 --> 00:08:51.608
Please sing it for us! say the TV men.

00:08:51.668 --> 00:08:54.419
But Zapp smiles.

00:08:54.479 --> 00:09:02.198
No, no — you must come to my big concert next Saturday.

00:09:02.258 --> 00:09:06.916
He puts the CD in his pocket again.

00:09:06.976 --> 00:09:14.290
Now let’s go on the Zapp-o-copter! says Zapp.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:18.624
He sees a teacher with some children.

00:09:18.684 --> 00:09:21.836
Would they like to come too?

00:09:21.896 --> 00:09:23.846
He asks her.

00:09:23.906 --> 00:09:28.160
Of course, says the teacher.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:32.704
They help the children into the helicopters.

00:09:32.764 --> 00:09:36.977
Zapp smiles and smiles.

00:09:37.037 --> 00:09:41.618
The photographers take lots of pictures.

00:09:41.678 --> 00:09:45.548
Photo Phil arrives too.

00:09:45.608 --> 00:09:49.619
He is one of the Happy Hills characters.

00:09:49.679 --> 00:09:55.720
He takes a photo of the children — and sprays them with water!

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.821
Everybody laughs.

00:09:58.881 --> 00:10:03.290
Zapp is having a wonderful day.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:07.010
He speaks to the TV people.

00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:12.706
The photographers take photos of him with all the characters.

00:10:12.766 --> 00:10:16.188
Zapp meets Charlie Clown.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:22.534
Charlie gives him a flower — and the flower sprays him with water.

00:10:22.594 --> 00:10:25.647
Everybody laughs.

00:10:25.707 --> 00:10:32.041
Sally meets Zapp too, and she is very excited.

00:10:32.101 --> 00:10:37.901
But she cannot talk to him because she is wearing her cat costume.

00:10:37.961 --> 00:10:43.562
And Mr Parry is watching.

00:10:43.623 --> 00:10:55.800
Chapter Four. Where’s Zapp’s CD?

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:01.320
Come on, it’s eleven o’clock, says William.
 
00:11:01.380 --> 00:11:04.625
Let’s go to the canteen for our break.

00:11:04.685 --> 00:11:07.506
We’ve got ten minutes.

00:11:07.566 --> 00:11:13.508
They sit down in the canteen and take off their heads.

00:11:13.568 --> 00:11:16.208
Sally is thirsty.

00:11:16.268 --> 00:11:19.539
Her face is hot and red.

00:11:19.599 --> 00:11:23.640
William is hot and thirsty too.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.062
They have a long drink of cold water.

00:11:28.122 --> 00:11:30.724
That’s good!

00:11:30.784 --> 00:11:32.867
William says.

00:11:32.927 --> 00:11:36.300
Then he looks at his watch.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:40.700
Ten past eleven, he says.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.729
Come on, Sally.

00:11:42.789 --> 00:11:45.390
Back to work!

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:51.290
They finish their drinks and put their heads on again.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:55.861
Suddenly a lot of people come into the canteen.

00:11:55.881 --> 00:12:01.073
What’s the matter? says William.

00:12:01.133 --> 00:12:06.166
Zapp’s CD! says Mr Parry.

00:12:06.226 --> 00:12:09.268
He can’t find it!

00:12:09.328 --> 00:12:12.900
Everybody is unhappy.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:16.892
But Zapp is angry too.

00:12:16.952 --> 00:12:21.294
That CD’s important, Parry,

00:12:21.354 --> 00:12:25.636
he says. You must find it.

00:12:25.696 --> 00:12:31.231
I’m doing my best, Zapp, says Mr Parry.

00:12:31.291 --> 00:12:33.814
Don’t hit me, please —

00:12:33.874 --> 00:12:37.388
I’m doing my best!

00:12:37.448 --> 00:12:42.352
A lot of things happen very quickly.

00:12:42.412 --> 00:12:45.884
The visitors want to go home.

00:12:45.944 --> 00:12:51.028
but suddenly Mr Parry closes all the doors.

00:12:51.088 --> 00:12:55.240
Nobody can leave, he says. 

00:12:55.300 --> 00:13:01.010
I’m sorry, but Zapp’s CD’s very important

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:04.297
and we must find it.

00:13:04.357 --> 00:13:09.008
Mr Parry makes a telephone call.

00:13:09.068 --> 00:13:15.430
Very soon four police arrive in a big white police car.

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:19.290
They ask a lot of questions.

00:13:19.350 --> 00:13:24.042
The police look everywhere for the CD.

00:13:24.102 --> 00:13:28.151
They read Mr Parry’s list of visitors.

00:13:28.211 --> 00:13:35.601
They count the visitors carefully and look in all their pockets and bags.

00:13:35.661 --> 00:13:38.892
There is a lot of noise.

00:13:38.952 --> 00:13:42.483
People are angry and tired.

00:13:42.543 --> 00:13:45.674
They want to go home now.

00:13:45.734 --> 00:13:53.416
And Zapp is speaking very quietly into a little black telephone.

00:13:53.476 --> 00:14:00.178
Photo Phil goes to him and says, Smile, please!

00:14:00.238 --> 00:14:06.320
Go away! says Zapp angrily.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:11.120
Now the police want to talk to the workers.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:18.962
One stays with the visitors and three police speak to the workers in the canteen.

00:14:19.022 --> 00:14:22.423
Zapp comes with the police.

00:14:22.483 --> 00:14:28.414
You must find that CD! says Zapp.

00:14:28.474 --> 00:14:31.434
We’re doing our best, Zapp,

00:14:31.494 --> 00:14:35.546
say the police.

00:14:35.606 --> 00:14:47.370
Chapter Five. The Fifteenth Character. 

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:53.008
Sally waits quietly with the other workers.

00:14:53.068 --> 00:15:00.899
She looks at Mr Parry’s Jobs for Today list and counts the names.

00:15:00.959 --> 00:15:05.062
There are twenty-nine names on the list today.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:09.826
Fifteen people are helpers.

00:15:09.886 --> 00:15:16.732
They wear green trousers and yellow shirts and help the visitors.

00:15:16.792 --> 00:15:24.387
Fourteen people are characters and wear costumes.

00:15:24.447 --> 00:15:29.829
Wait a minute, thinks Sally.
 
00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:33.551
There are fourteen characters on the list.

00:15:33.612 --> 00:15:37.954
But there are fifteen characters here!

00:15:38.014 --> 00:15:44.308
She reads the list again very, very carefully.

00:15:44.368 --> 00:15:49.610
Edward Elephant — yes, he’s here.
 
00:15:49.671 --> 00:15:54.046
Connie Cat — that’s me.
  
00:15:54.106 --> 00:15:58.741
Cowboy Joe — that’s William.
 
00:15:58.801 --> 00:16:03.592
Photo Phil — yes, he’s here.
 
00:16:03.652 --> 00:16:07.643
Big Apple — yes.
 
00:16:07.703 --> 00:16:15.995
Sir Laugh-a-Lot and Lady Love-a-Little… Wait a minute.
 
00:16:16.055 --> 00:16:19.446
Charlie Clown isn’t on the list —

00:16:19.506 --> 00:16:23.954
but Charlie’s here in this room!

00:16:24.014 --> 00:16:29.124
Excuse me, Mr Parry, says Sally.

00:16:29.184 --> 00:16:33.050
There are fourteen characters on your list, 

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:36.770
but there are fifteen in the room now.

00:16:36.829 --> 00:16:42.034
Charlie Clown isn’t on the list, but he’s here.

00:16:42.094 --> 00:16:48.089
Mr Parry reads the list and counts the characters.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:53.492
You’re right, Sally, he says.

00:16:53.552 --> 00:16:56.872
Take off your heads!

00:16:56.932 --> 00:17:00.384
Mr Parry says to the characters.

00:17:00.444 --> 00:17:04.026
They take off their heads.

00:17:04.085 --> 00:17:08.547
Charlie Clown is a woman.

00:17:08.608 --> 00:17:12.920
Why are you wearing that costume?

00:17:12.981 --> 00:17:15.582
asks Mr Parry.

00:17:15.642 --> 00:17:19.373
The woman begins to run away.

00:17:19.434 --> 00:17:22.524
But William stops her.

00:17:22.584 --> 00:17:29.336
The police take off her costume — and find a big pocket.

00:17:29.396 --> 00:17:33.269
In it they find Zapp's CD.

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:37.652
The singer smiles again.

00:17:37.712 --> 00:17:41.216
It is Saturday night.

00:17:41.276 --> 00:17:48.361
Sally and William are in London because they are going to Zapp's concert.

00:17:48.421 --> 00:17:55.637
There are lots of excited people and TV photographers outside the hall.

00:17:55.697 --> 00:18:00.821
Everybody wants to hear Zapp's new song.

00:18:00.881 --> 00:18:04.154
Where are your tickets?

00:18:04.214 --> 00:18:08.246
says the man at the door to Sally.

00:18:08.306 --> 00:18:13.890
We haven’t got any tickets, says Sally.

00:18:13.951 --> 00:18:18.006
The man begins to look angry.

00:18:18.067 --> 00:18:24.341
Sally smiles and takes something out of her pocket.

00:18:24.401 --> 00:18:27.938
Is this invitation OK?

00:18:27.999 --> 00:18:39.321
It’s from Zapp.